{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-004-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRenderTraceTests.cs","line":228,"method":"EmitRaw_Important_RoutesToInfoWithPhaseAndSurfaceTokens","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRenderTrace.cs:1490; swap ParsekLog.Info for ParsekLog.Verbose in EmitRaw -> all three Info-routing tests stay GREEN today, red once the level token is asserted","what_it_asserts":"That the emitted line carries phase/surface/pid/detail tokens under the [MapRenderTrace] tag.","why_weak":"The three tests whose names claim Info routing assert no level token, and the fixture sets VerboseOverrideForTesting=true, so a Verbose-routed line matches every predicate. Info routing is the whole point of important=true (it survives verboseLogging off, per EmitFactoryParity_MismatchLandsWithVerboseLoggingDisabled).","proposed_action":"Add l.Contains(\"[INFO]\") to EmitRaw_Important_RoutesToInfoWithPhaseAndSurfaceTokens, EmitStructural_GhostCreated_RoutesToInfoAndOpensWindow and EmitStructural_FirstPosition_RoutesToInfoWithOrbitFields (ParsekLog.Write formats [Parsek][LEVEL][Subsystem]).","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-004-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRenderTraceTests.cs","line":526,"method":"EmitWindowSnapshot_NoOpWhenDisabled","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRenderTrace.cs:1545; delete EmitWindowSnapshot's IsEnabled guard -> test stays GREEN (no window was ever opened), red only after the arrange opens the window with tracing on","what_it_asserts":"That a disabled tracer logs nothing from EmitWindowSnapshot.","why_weak":"The comment states 'even if a window were somehow open', but OpenDetailedWindow is itself IsEnabled-gated, so the window is never opened and the no-op is decided by IsDetailedWindowOpen, not by the guard the test names. Same redundant-gate shape in EmitStructural_NoOpWhenDisabled, EmitFactoryParity_Disabled_NoOp, EmitMarkerDecisionOnChange_NoOpWhenDisabled, EmitLineVisibilityOnChange_NoOpWhenDisabled.","proposed_action":"Arrange with ForceEnabledForTesting=true, OpenDetailedWindow, then set ForceEnabledForTesting=false before calling EmitWindowSnapshot, so the guard under test is the only thing preventing the line.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"MapRenderTrace.MarkerRideReasonToken","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/MapRenderTrace.cs","sut_line":346,"case_kind":"boundary","proposed_name":"MarkerRideReasonToken_HeldLastGoodAndNonAnchored_CarryTokens","sketch":"Assert MarkerRideReasonToken(HeldLastGood, 4) == \"held-last-good-leg4\" and MarkerRideReasonToken(FallbackNonAnchoredUseHead, -1) == \"fallback-non-anchored-use-head\".","guards":"The two newest MarkerRideReason members are unpinned; a renamed or index-dropping token would silently break the marker-decision grep contract.","risk":"ui"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"MapRenderTrace.BuildMarkerDecisionSignature","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/MapRenderTrace.cs","sut_line":402,"case_kind":"boundary","proposed_name":"BuildMarkerDecisionSignature_TsSkipReason_AppendedLastAndOmittedWhenEmpty","sketch":"Build one signature with tsSkipReason null and one with \"atmospheric-no-points\"; assert the null case is byte-identical to the flight signature and the non-null case ends with \" tsSkip=atmospheric-no-points\".","guards":"The C-1 tsSkip field contract (appended LAST so FLIGHT signatures stay byte-identical) is untested; a field-order change would shift every TS signature and break change-detection dedup.","risk":"ui"}
